<title>UK: Legal &amp; General inches up after income data.</title>
<headline>Legal &amp; General inches up after income data.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Legal &amp; General Plc were 1-1/2p higher at 394p by 0900 GMT after the insurance group said that new UK equivalent premium income rose 54 percent in 1996 to 301 million stg.</p>
<p>The company also said all product areas showed significant growth.</p>
<p>&quot;Legal &amp; General is a market favourite at the moment. A lot of people think it will either be taken over or merge with a larger financial services group,&quot; the head of trading and sales at a large investment bank said.</p>
<p>&quot;These figures are just icing on the cake.&quot;</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
